{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e5a-32bc-7443-a1f1-5c57fcb17017"},"sequence":195,"recorded_at":1780531400000385,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"8cd46f03-5e83-4b8e-bd79-63afeddb504b"},"task_id":"8cd46f03-5e83-4b8e-bd79-63afeddb504b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"8cd46f03-5e83-4b8e-bd79-63afeddb504b","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-9-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"4\\\\.A\\\\|4\\\\.1\\\\|§4\\\\|TerminalBackend\\\\|backend\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.md | head -n 60; echo \\\"===\\\"; wc -l internal/specdoc/SPEC.md; wc -l internal/specpin/*.go internal/specdoc/*.go\",\n  \"description\": \"Find backend spec sections\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"39:   terminal backend supports it, a reboot;\\n82:| Unix terminal backend | PTY management plus tmux integration on macOS, Linux, or WSL2 |\\n83:| Windows terminal backend | Native PowerShell process supervision and ConPTY; no tmux claim |\\n122:| Configuration | <code>urn:ax:schema:config</code> | <code>1.0.0</code>, <code>2.0.0</code> for directory-capable installations, <code>3.0.0</code> for TerminalBackend selection and policy |\\n126:| Terminal Backend protocol | <code>urn:ax:protocol:terminal-backend</code> | <code>1.0.0</code> |\\n127:| Terminal Backend manifest | <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-manifest</code> | <code>1.0.0</code> |\\n128:| Terminal Backend probe | <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-probe</code> | <code>1.0.0</code> |\\n138:| Mesh RPC | <code>urn:ax:protocol:rpc</code> | <code>2.0.0</code>, <code>3.0.0</code> for directory replication, <code>4.0.0</code> for sanitized TerminalBackend evidence replication |\\n155:| Structured error | <code>urn:ax:schema:error</code> | <code>1.0.0</code>, <code>1.1.0</code> for cloning, <code>1.2.0</code> for directory surfaces, <code>1.3.0</code> for TerminalBackend surfaces |\\n157:| CLI result | <code>urn:ax:schema:cli-result</code> | <code>1.0.0</code>, <code>2.0.0</code> for <code>session.clone.*</code>, <code>3.0.0</code> for <code>sessions.*</code> commands, <code>4.0.0</code> for TerminalBackend commands and generalized start/resume results |\\n374:| Provider identity | Provider ID, native durable handle, logical workspace mapping, and non-secret backend-realm fingerprint needed to resolve a native session. |\\n379:| Native session instance | One provider-native durable session in one backend realm on one host; it is not an AX logical Session until validated binding or adoption creates that authority. |\\n677:- <strong>terminal backend</strong>: tmux/PTTY on Unix-family systems or\\n717:Container, and TerminalBackend Component views, including the Directory Control\\n719:boundary, AX Terminal Controller/Registry, host-local backend boundary, tmux and\\n722:continuation, and TerminalBackend authority/lifecycle flows MUST be rendered as\\n770:On macOS the tmux backend MUST use a dedicated AX server selected by\\n862:### 4.A TerminalBackend authority and terminology\\n864:TerminalBackend is a host-local presentation and delegated process-hosting\\n868:replication, and takeover. A backend owns exactly one host-local\\n870:attach/reconnect, backend-local IPC, and backend-specific process observation.\\n879:Every backend-created runtime ultimately executes exactly\\n881:durable entry point. A backend MUST NOT interpret ownership, start or resume a\\n885:destination backend without clone or fork; AX emits a new immutable binding,\\n890:<code>terminal_backend_id</code> is 1–128 ASCII bytes matching\\n901:| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-manifest</code> |\\n904:| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\\n910:| <code>static_capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] whose <code>origin</code> is <code>static</code> |\\n919:| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-probe</code> |\\n922:| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\\n930:| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest of the domain-separated raw generation |\\n931:| <code>capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] |\\n937:<code>ax-terminal-backend-generation-v1\\\\0</code> followed by the backend's\\n940:Probe <code>terminal_backend_id</code>, <code>implementation_version</code>,\\n986:<code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code> and fails before\\n998:stable public SDK is deferred until tmux and one materially different backend\\n1008:<code>urn:ax:protocol:terminal-backend</code>,\\n1031:| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\\n1034:| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256]; this is the canonical bound in every containing contract |\\n1035:| <code>native_reference</code> | sanitized opaque string[1..512], meaningful only to this backend on this host incarnation |\\n1054:idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\\n1064:<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\\n1065:<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\\n1071:TerminalBackendSideEffect.\\n1079:backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\\n1101:<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\\n1103:<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\\n1111:<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\\n1113:<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\\n1116:<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\\n1131:| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\\n1132:| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\\\|linux\\\\|wsl2\\\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\\n1134:| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\\n1135:| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\\n1143:<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\\n1145:<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\\n1159:An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\\n1161:<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\\n1166:| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\\n1167:| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\\n===\\n   12665 internal/specdoc/SPEC.md\\n     233 internal/specpin/pin_test.go\\n     336 internal/specpin/pin.go\\n     160 internal/specpin/scope_test.go\\n     189 internal/specpin/sections.go\\n     223 internal/specdoc/embed_reach_test.go\\n     429 internal/specdoc/specdoc_test.go\\n     385 internal/specdoc/specdoc.go\\n    1955 total\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8049,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2013,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
