{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4f9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e5a-32bc-7443-a1f1-5c57fcb17017"},"sequence":215,"recorded_at":1780531400000425,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc"},"call_id":"call_01a06e5aac1073a39e3e75d8533fe40a","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(861 line(s) above)\n862|### 4.A TerminalBackend authority and terminology\n863|\n864|TerminalBackend is a host-local presentation and delegated process-hosting\n865|module. AX alone owns Logical Session identity and lineage, Owner and AX\n866|Replica roles, leases and fencing, provider lifecycle/native identity/store,\n867|workspace materialization, Checkpoints/evidence, task-board integration, mesh\n868|replication, and takeover. A backend owns exactly one host-local\n869|<dfn>Terminal Instance</dfn>: delegated PTY/process hosting, presentation,\n870|attach/reconnect, backend-local IPC, and backend-specific process observation.\n871|\n872|An <dfn>AX Replica</dfn> is a host holding synchronized durable AX state. A\n873|<dfn>presentation replica</dfn> or <dfn>client mirror</dfn> is only a view/input\n874|client of one Terminal Instance. Presentation replication MUST NOT create an AX\n875|Replica, acquire or renew a lease, change Owner, authorize input, or publish an\n876|owner-authored event. Schemas, CLI, UI, and logs MUST NOT use these terms\n877|interchangeably.\n878|\n879|Every backend-created runtime ultimately executes exactly\n880|<code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>; a raw provider command is forbidden as a\n881|durable entry point. A backend MUST NOT interpret ownership, start or resume a\n882|provider without AX authorization, replace AX/provider/workspace/Checkpoint/\n883|task-board/mesh state, or turn attach into a lease mutation. A valid takeover\n884|or owner resume MAY bind the same Logical Session to a different conforming\n885|destination backend without clone or fork; AX emits a new immutable binding,\n886|event, and evidence and never mutates history.\n887|\n888|### 4.B Registry, identity, discovery, and trust\n889|\n890|<code>terminal_backend_id</code> is 1–128 ASCII bytes matching\n891|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:[.-][a-z0-9]+)*</code>. The <code>ax.</code> namespace is\n892|reserved. Canonical built-ins are <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n893|<code>ax.conpty</code>. Third parties use a stable vendor-owned namespace. No\n894|normative Superlogical ID is reserved.\n895|\n896|Terminal Backend Manifest 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no\n897|other member is permitted:\n898|\n899|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n900|| --- | --- |\n901|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-manifest</code> |\n902|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n903|| <code>manifest_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n904|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n905|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver |\n906|| <code>protocol_versions</code> | sorted unique semver[1..32], each in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n907|| <code>platforms</code> | sorted unique enum[1..4] from <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> |\n908|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | <code>builtin_go|local_program|trusted_executable|native_runtime</code> |\n909|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest for <code>local_program</code> or <code>trusted_executable</code>; null otherwise |\n910|| <code>static_capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] whose <code>origin</code> is <code>static</code> |\n911|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest |\n912|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code>; non-empty extensions require a later contract version |\n913|\n914|Terminal Backend Probe 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable observation; no\n915|other member is permitted:\n916|\n917|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n918|| --- | --- |\n919|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-probe</code> |\n920|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n921|| <code>probe_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n922|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n923|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to the admitted Manifest |\n924|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver selected from the Manifest's <code>protocol_versions</code> |\n925|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | enum equal to the Manifest member |\n926|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest|null exactly equal to the Manifest member |\n927|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code>, contained in the Manifest's <code>platforms</code> |\n928|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] |\n929|| <code>availability</code> | <code>available|conditional|unavailable|unknown</code> |\n930|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest of the domain-separated raw generation |\n931|| <code>capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] |\n932|| <code>evidence_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..256] referencing Capability Evidence 1.0.0 |\n933|| <code>probed_at</code> | timestamp |\n934|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n935|\n936|The generation digest uses SHA-256 over UTF-8\n937|<code>ax-terminal-backend-generation-v1\\0</code> followed by the backend's\n938|host-local raw generation bytes; it neither reveals nor reconstructs that\n939|generation. Manifest-to-Probe reconciliation is the following closed rule. The\n940|Probe <code>terminal_backend_id</code>, <code>implementation_version</code>,\n941|<code>implementation_kind</code>, and <code>executable_digest</code> MUST equal\n942|the Manifest members; its <code>protocol_version</code> MUST be exactly one member\n943|of <code>protocol_versions</code>, and its <code>platform</code> MUST be exactly\n944|one member of <code>platforms</code>. Array-to-scalar selection is membership,\n945|not aggregate equality.\n946|\n947|Let <code>M[c]</code> be the one Manifest static claim for capability\n948|<code>c</code>, when present, and <code>P[c]</code> the one Probe claim. The\n949|declared sorted-unique constraints make a duplicate key invalid before this\n950|reconciliation runs. The complete keyed relation is:\n951|\n952|1. Every <code>M[c]</code> MUST have exactly one <code>P[c]</code>; omission is a\n953|   manifest/probe mismatch.\n954|2. <code>P[c].origin=static</code> is permitted only when <code>M[c]</code>\n955|   exists, and <code>P[c]</code> MUST then equal <code>M[c]</code> member for\n956|   member. It is a static echo, not a new observation.\n957|3. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> with an existing <code>M[c]</code> is a\n958|   generation-bound override. It is permitted only when\n959|   <code>M[c].generation_variable=true</code>; its <code>value</code> MAY differ,\n960|   while <code>generation_variable</code>, <code>dependent_operations</code>, and\n961|   <code>evidence_requirements</code> MUST remain equal to <code>M[c]</code> and\n962|   the capability registry row.\n963|4. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> without <code>M[c]</code> is a probed\n964|   addition. It is permitted only for a capability in the closed registry, and\n965|   its three registry-derived members MUST equal that row. A Probe cannot add\n966|   a claim with <code>origin=static</code>.\n967|5. A true <code>P[c]</code> is admitted only when unexpired Capability Evidence\n968|   bound to this exact Manifest/Probe tuple satisfies every listed evidence\n969|   requirement. The required fact mapping is\n970|   <code>conformance_fixture-&gt;fixture_passed</code>,\n971|   <code>runtime_probe-&gt;runtime_probe_passed</code>,\n972|   <code>credential_sentinel-&gt;sentinel_passed</code>,\n973|   <code>provider_auth_smoke-&gt;provider_auth_passed</code>, and\n974|   <code>policy_authorization-&gt;policy_checked</code>. A false claim has no\n975|   matching Capability Evidence because Evidence <code>value</code> is the\n976|   literal <code>true</code>.\n977|6. <code>evidence_ids</code> MUST be exactly the sorted unique IDs of all\n978|   returned Capability Evidence objects used by true <code>P</code> claims.\n979|   Every referenced object MUST name exactly one present true claim; an ID for\n980|   an absent or false claim, an unreferenced returned object, conflicting\n981|   evidence, or duplicate/conflicting claims invalidates the whole Probe.\n982|\n983|A partial, malformed, stale, or failed Manifest, Probe, or evidence read is an\n984|error, never absence or availability. Any failed equality, membership, keyed\n985|relation, evidence binding, or evidence coverage rule is\n986|<code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code> and fails before\n987|activation; executable substitution or implementation drift additionally maps\n988|to its more specific Section 15.3 code.\n989|\n990|Discovery completes before activation. Duplicate/ambiguous IDs,\n991|manifest/probe disagreement, implementation drift, untrusted executable\n992|substitution, stale generation, unknown identity/version, or unevidenced claims\n993|fail closed. A manifest is not availability proof. External adapters use argv\n994|and local length-prefixed framing: unsigned 32-bit big-endian byte length plus\n995|UTF-8 JSON, at most 1 MiB, one request/response at a time. EOF, oversize,\n996|invalid JSON, unsolicited output, or deadline expiry terminates the adapter.\n997|M0 exposes only an internal semantic interface and conformance harness; a\n998|stable public SDK is deferred until tmux and one materially different backend\n999|validate the boundary.\n1000|\n1001|Manifest, Probe, Binding, and Capability Evidence IDs equal the lowercase\n1002|<code>sha256:</code> digest of RFC 8785 JCS bytes with their own ID member\n1003|omitted. A reader MUST recompute the ID before use. Manifest and Probe remain\n1004|immutable observations when later probes supersede them.\n1005|\n1006|Terminal Backend Protocol 1.0.0 has a closed request envelope containing\n1007|exactly <code>protocol</code> with literal\n1008|<code>urn:ax:protocol:terminal-backend</code>,\n1009|<code>protocol_version</code> with exact value <code>1.0.0</code>,\n1010|<code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>operation</code>, and <code>body</code>.\n1011|Its response repeats those three identity members exactly and contains\n1012|<code>ok:true,result:&lt;operation-success-body&gt;</code> or\n1013|<code>ok:false,error:StructuredError1.3</code>, never both result and error.\n1014|Operation is one of the ten names in Section 4.C and the exact bodies are its\n1015|typed matrix. Unknown members, operations, or body variants are protocol\n1016|errors. This is an AX-controlled local adapter wire, not a stable public SDK.\n1017|\n1018|AX allocates <code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>. Terminal Instance Binding\n1019|1.0.0 is the following closed immutable host-local object; no other member is\n1020|permitted:\n1021|\n1022|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1023|| --- | --- |\n1024|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding</code> |\n1025|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1026|| <code>binding_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule above |\n1027|| <code>session_id</code> | Logical Session UUIDv7 |\n1028|| <code>host_id</code> | AX Host UUIDv7 |\n1029|| <code>host_incarnation_id</code> | UUIDv7 allocated once for the current host-agent process incarnation |\n1030|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-allocated UUIDv7 |\n1031|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1032|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to admitted Manifest and Probe |\n1033|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1, equal to the Probe |\n1034|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256]; this is the canonical bound in every containing contract |\n1035|| <code>native_reference</code> | sanitized opaque string[1..512], meaningful only to this backend on this host incarnation |\n1036|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp |\n1037|| <code>supersedes_binding_id</code> | digest|null; null only for the first binding of this Session on this host incarnation |\n1038|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1039|\n1040|Identity MUST NOT be a PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token, or\n1041|mutable endpoint. Binding is host/incarnation-local and does not alter Logical\n1042|Session identity. Boundary conformance cases MUST reject generation lengths 0\n1043|and 257 and accept length 256 in the Binding, Provider Protocol 3 descriptor,\n1044|operation bodies, and CLI Result 4 summary.\n1045|\n1046|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n1047|\n1048|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n1049|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n1050|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n1051|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n1052|\n1053|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n1054|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n1055|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n1056|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n1057|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n1058|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n1059|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n1060|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n1061|\n1062|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n1063|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n1064|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1065|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n1066|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n1067|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n1068|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n1069|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n1070|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1071|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n1072|\n1073|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n1074|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n1075|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n1076|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n1077|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n1078|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n1079|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n1080|\n1081|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1082|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n1083|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1084|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n1085|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1086|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n1087|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n1088|\n1089|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n1090|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n1091|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1092|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n1093|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1094|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n1095|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n1096|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n1097|\n1098|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1099|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1100|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1101|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1102|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1103|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1104|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n1105|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n1106|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n1107|\n1108|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1109|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1110|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1111|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1112|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1113|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1114|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1115|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1116|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n1117|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n1118|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n1119|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n1120|\n1121|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n1122|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n1123|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n1124|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n1125|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n1126|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n1127|persisted or replicated.\n1128|\n1129|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n1130|| --- | --- | --- |\n1131|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n1132|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n1133|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n1134|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n1135|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n1136|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1137|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1138|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n1139|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n1140|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n1141|\n1142|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n1143|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n1144|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n1145|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n1146|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n1147|<code>identity_match:false</code>, <code>state:absent</code>,\n1148|<code>wrapper_present:false</code>, <code>provider_present:null</code>,\n1149|<code>attachable:false</code>, and both last fields null; it does not authorize\n1150|fallback. <code>provider_present</code> is null unless provider observation was\n1151|requested and evidenced. <code>attachable</code> is true only in\n1152|<code>parked|active</code> with a currently evidenced matching attach\n1153|capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the\n1154|request and AttachAuthorization; <code>attach_descriptor</code> in\n1155|<code>create</code> is non-null exactly when <code>interactive</code> is true.\n1156|\n1157|The following table is the exact transition, authorization, idempotency,\n1158|deadline/recovery, evidence, capability, and Structured Error 1.3 mapping.\n1159|An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\n1160|syntactically valid request; AX-local parsing may additionally emit\n1161|<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\n1162|transition and no side effect.\n1163|\n1164|| Operation | Allowed source → success state; exact side effects | Authorization and idempotency key | Deadline/lost-result recovery and required evidence | Capability dependencies | Allowed error codes |\n1165|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1166|| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1167|| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1168|| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1169|| <code>attach</code> | <code>parked</code> → <code>active</code> or <code>active</code> → <code>active</code>; <code>attach_client_created</code> | valid unexpired AttachAuthorization equal to request transport/input; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/\" + client_id</code> | timeout creates no authorized input unless the durable client receipt says so; retry same client ID; attach-policy/capability evidence | matching <code>local_attach|remote_attach|web_attach</code>; <code>multi_attach</code> for overlap; <code>multiple_input_clients</code> plus AX policy for concurrent input | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1170|| <code>status</code> | <code>absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → same state; none | none; key is full queried identity tuple | timeout/read failure is unknown, never absent; retry query; status evidence IDs only | <code>provider_process_observation</code> exactly when provider observation requested | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1171|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>active|parked</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>input_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation</code> | receipt precedes input closure; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; evidence binds closure time/generation | <code>input_quiescence</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1172|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>safe_boundary_observed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind</code> | lesser of request deadline and timeout; identical retry returns the same proof; no proof on timeout; safe-boundary evidence | <code>safe_boundary_observation</code>; also <code>provider_process_observation</code> for provider proof kinds | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1173|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>graceful_stop_requested,process_closed,backend_store_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id</code> | lesser deadline/timeout; lost result requires <code>status</code>, then same-key retry only if not closed; boundary and closure evidence | <code>graceful_stop</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1174|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>stale_incarnation_terminated,process_closed</code> | <code>force_stale</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/terminate/\" + stale_lease_id + \"/\" + decimal(stale_epoch)</code> | deadline may leave uncertain closure; use <code>status</code> before same-key retry; diagnostic, fencing, and closure evidence | <code>stale_process_termination</code> and <code>provider_process_observation</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1175|| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1176|\n1177|Create is idempotent on <code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code> across\n1178|controller crash and lost result. AX and backend durably bind the pair before\n1179|the first child side effect. Identical retry returns the one result/instance;\n1180|a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n1181|Only a successful status read proves absence. Attach is ownership-observational\n1182|for current-owner resume, local/remote/web, reconnect, and multi-attach.\n1183|\n1184|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n1185|\n1186|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\n1187|<dfn>TerminalBackendOperation</dfn> is exactly\n1188|<code>manifest|probe|create|attach|status|quiesce-input|wait-safe-boundary|request-stop|terminate-stale|restore</code>.\n1189|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceRequirement</dfn> is exactly\n1190|<code>conformance_fixture|runtime_probe|credential_sentinel|provider_auth_smoke|policy_authorization</code>.\n1191|\n1192|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1193|<code>capability:TerminalBackendCapability</code>,\n1194|<code>origin:static|probed</code>, <code>value:boolean</code>,\n1195|<code>generation_variable:boolean</code>,\n1196|<code>dependent_operations:sorted-unique TerminalBackendOperation[1..10]</code>,\n1197|and <code>evidence_requirements:sorted-unique CapabilityEvidenceRequirement[1..5]</code>.\n1198|The latter three members MUST exactly equal the registry row for the capability;\n1199|a Manifest or Probe cannot redefine them. A false claim is retained to make a\n1200|probed refusal explicit but confers no operation.\n1201|\n1202|| Capability | Exact semantics | Generation-variable | Exact dependent operations | Exact evidence requirements |\n1203|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1204|| <code>durable_disconnect</code> | Wrapper survives every client disconnect. | false | <code>create,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1205|| <code>local_attach</code> | Local-only presentation. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1206|| <code>remote_attach</code> | Presentation over trusted private mesh only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1207|| <code>web_attach</code> | Web presentation over an admitted transport only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1208|| <code>multi_attach</code> | Concurrent presentation clients; no multi-input or ownership implication. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1209|| <code>headless_creation</code> | Create without UI or prompt in the proven execution realm. | true | <code>create</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1210|| <code>reboot_restoration</code> | Re-establish after reboot; does not claim process survival. | true | <code>restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1211|| <code>input_quiescence</code> | Reject new input with generation-bound evidence. | true | <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1212|| <code>safe_boundary_observation</code> | Observe AX/provider-selected safe-boundary proof. | true | <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1213|| <code>provider_process_observation</code> | Observe provider presence without PID identity. | true | <code>status,terminate-stale,wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1214|| <code>graceful_stop</code> | Request and observe orderly exit. | true | <code>request-stop</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1215|| <code>stale_process_termination</code> | Target one fenced stale incarnation. | true | <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1216|| <code>terminal_state_retention</code> | Retain local presentation state, never portable Checkpoint state. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1217|| <code>scrollback_retention</code> | Retain local scrollback, never replicated terminal output. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1218|| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\n1219|| <code>multiple_input_clients</code> | Backend serializes multiple input clients; AX policy separately authorizes use. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1220|\n1221|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceFact</dfn> is the exact enum\n1222|<code>fixture_passed|runtime_probe_passed|sentinel_passed|provider_auth_passed|policy_checked|ui_absent|prompt_absent</code>.\n1223|Capability Evidence 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no other\n1224|member is permitted:\n1225|\n1226|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1227|| --- | --- |\n1228|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence</code> |\n1229|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1230|| <code>evidence_id</code> | digest computed by the Section 4.B identity rule |\n1231|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1232|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to Manifest and Probe |\n1233|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver equal to Probe |\n1234|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest equal to Probe |\n1235|| <code>capability</code> | TerminalBackendCapability |\n1236|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n1237|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n1238|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n1239|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n1240|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n1241|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n1242|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n1243|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n1244|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n1245|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n1246|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1247|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1248|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1249|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1250|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1251|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1252|\n1253|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n1254|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n1255|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n1256|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n1257|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n1258|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n1259|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n1260|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n1261|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n1262|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n1263|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n1264|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n1265|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n1266|change and before activation.\n1267|\n1268|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n1269|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n1270|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n1271|activation when policy allows.\n1272|\n1273|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n1274|\n1275|| Classification | Members and rule |\n1276|| --- | --- |\n1277|| Safe immutable evidence | Sanitized backend identity/version/platform/conformance/capability evidence; MAY persist and replicate after validation. |\n1278|| Host-local durable metadata | Instance/binding IDs, sanitized native reference, generation, idempotency receipt, last effect; host-local, non-replicable. |\n1279|| Derived cache | Discovery/availability/attachability/process observations and probe views; rebuildable, non-authoritative. |\n1280|| Sensitive runtime state | IPC, tmux sockets, named pipes, attach/relay credentials, backend auth/live databases, GUI/login attestations, provider credentials; owner-only and non-replicable. |\n1281|| Forbidden | Raw native reference, PID/handle, endpoint/token, terminal output/scrollback, unrestricted environment, credential detail, and live-process facts MUST NOT replicate. |\n1282|\n1283|Presentation transport is exactly <code>local_only</code>,\n1284|<code>trusted_private_mesh</code>, or <code>third_party_relay</code>. Current AX\n1285|admits only the first two. A relay-required/public-service backend is unavailable\n1286|pending explicit future product/contract approval. AX retains no permanent\n1287|public TCP listener. Attach transport carries no AX authoritative state,\n1288|provider store, workspace, Checkpoint, task-board data, or ownership change.\n1289|\n1290|The exact v0.4.3 Configuration 1/2 <code>tmux|conpty</code>, Provider Protocol 2\n1291|TerminalDescriptor, Session Event 1 terminal payloads, and CLI Result 1 start/\n1292|resume shapes and digests remain immutable. Version adapters deterministically\n1293|map legacy <code>tmux</code> to <code>ax.tmux</code> and <code>conpty</code> to\n1294|<code>ax.conpty</code>, with version/generation <code>legacy_unreported</code>\n1295|and no inferred capabilities. Reverse projection exists only for those two IDs;\n1296|other IDs return <code>incompatible_schema</code>, never fallback. Translation\n1297|never rewrites or re-digests history.\n1298|\n1299|New readers accept old objects through the adapter. Old readers may browse/sync\n1300|opaque newer immutable records but cannot activate, restore, or write them.\n1301|Mixed peers negotiate each containing contract independently; no common backend\n1302|major means browse/sync only. Unknown/unsupported IDs remain visible as unknown/\n1303|unavailable; registry read failure is never absence. Lower-version writers are\n1304|read-only and cannot write downgrade replacements. Bootstrap permits only a\n1305|framed <code>manifest</code> call in an understood major. Capability negotiation\n1306|is the intersection plus valid bound evidence, never union or inference.\n1307|\n1308|Mesh RPC 4.0.0 is defined normatively in Section 11.9: its exact 25-key hello\n1309|map changes the RPC and Session Event arrays and adds exactly\n1310|<code>terminal_backend_evidence=[\"1.0.0\"]</code>; its exact eighth namespace\n1311|contains only sanitized Manifest, Probe, and Capability Evidence objects.\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
