{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c555","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e5a-32bc-7443-a1f1-5c57fcb17017"},"sequence":261,"recorded_at":1780531400000517,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"9dfe7896-d489-414c-a6ca-94b2f2e867a1"},"task_id":"9dfe7896-d489-414c-a6ca-94b2f2e867a1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"9dfe7896-d489-414c-a6ca-94b2f2e867a1","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(1337 line(s) above)\n1338|### 4.1 Terminal backend interface\n1339|\n1340|Every terminal backend MUST implement these semantic operations:\n1341|\n1342|| Operation | Required result |\n1343|| --- | --- |\n1344|| <code>create</code> | With <code>session_id</code> and caller-stable <code>bootstrap_operation_id</code>, create a durable pane/process whose only stable entry point is <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>. |\n1345|| <code>attach</code> | Connect an operator to the local terminal without changing ownership. |\n1346|| <code>status</code> | Report process presence, wrapper state, provider child state, and attachability. |\n1347|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | Stop new operator/provider input while retaining observation. |\n1348|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | Prove the adapter-specific safe boundary or time out. |\n1349|| <code>request-stop</code> | Ask the provider to exit through a version-tested graceful path. |\n1350|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | Terminate a process only for explicit force recovery after preserving diagnostics. |\n1351|| <code>restore</code> | Recreate the wrapper after reboot and consult current ownership before any provider resume. |\n1352|\n1353|The wrapper MUST validate configuration, load the logical session, synchronize\n1354|known lease records when possible, and compare the local fencing token before\n1355|launching a provider. It MUST park safely when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n1356|or unverified.\n1357|\n1358|Terminal creation and the wrapper's first child start are idempotent on\n1359|<code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code>. The backend MUST durably bind\n1360|that pair before child creation. An identical retry returns or reattaches to\n1361|the one recorded wrapper/child; changing the operation for a session still in\n1362|the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. After a lost result,\n1363|<code>status</code> plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one\n1364|child before any start retry. This contract never persists or replicates a PID\n1365|as identity.\n1366|\n1367|### 4.2 tmux backend\n1368|\n1369|On macOS, Linux, and WSL2, the supported durable terminal backend is tmux. Every\n1370|managed pane MUST run:\n1371|\n1372|~~~shell\n1373|ax pane <logical-session-id>\n1374|~~~\n1375|\n1376|It MUST NOT run the raw provider command as the pane's stable command.\n1377|<code>tmux-resurrect</code> plus <code>tmux-continuum</code> MAY recreate local\n1378|tmux layout and invoke the wrapper after reboot. They MUST NOT be described or\n1379|used as cross-host migration.\n1380|\n1381|AX MUST use its dedicated <code>-S</code> server and MUST NOT discover or reuse\n1382|the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name. On macOS, server\n1383|creation is credential-sensitive. A Background caller MUST NOT create a\n1384|credential-dependent tmux server. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon,\n1385|or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and\n1386|its attested AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return\n1387|<code>capability_unavailable</code> with typed realm/readiness details and MUST\n1388|NOT fall back to direct server creation.\n1389|\n1390|<code>launchctl managername</code> is a diagnostic hint only. Conformance\n1391|requires a functional AX sentinel inside the exact tmux server plus a separate\n1392|provider-auth smoke using the selected provider. Evidence MUST bind the exact\n1393|tmux server generation, provider build, and macOS version. Aqua alone and\n1394|sentinel-only evidence are insufficient. Any provider flow requiring GUI\n1395|interaction, Keychain UI, a permission prompt, or other human action fails\n1396|closed until that interaction succeeds in the verified GUI realm.\n1397|\n1398|After restore, the wrapper MUST:\n1399|\n1400|1. read the latest locally known lease;\n1401|2. attempt a mesh lease refresh without blocking forever;\n1402|3. resume locally only if the local host has the winning lease and the required\n1403|   materialization is valid;\n1404|4. offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session in an\n1405|   interactive terminal; or\n1406|5. enter <code>parked</code> without launching the provider in all other cases.\n1407|\n1408|Logout or reboot invalidates unrenewed realm evidence. Without a verified GUI\n1409|realm, recovery MUST remain parked until GUI login re-establishes the broker,\n1410|functional sentinel, provider-auth smoke, and their generation/build/version\n1411|binding. A cached sentinel or prior <code>managername</code> observation MUST\n1412|NOT authorize resume.\n1413|\n1414|### 4.3 Native Windows backend\n1415|\n1416|Native Windows PowerShell MUST use a Windows terminal backend implemented with\n1417|Go process supervision and ConPTY. It MUST support mesh sync, workspace and\n1418|provider materialization, direct/provider resume, task-board open/adopt, remote\n1419|attach, graceful takeover when the provider row passes ConPTY gates, force\n1420|takeover, stop, and continuation.\n1421|\n1422|Native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux or tmux resurrection. A reboot destroys the\n1423|live ConPTY. The user service MUST recreate <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>,\n1424|which resumes from the latest valid checkpoint only after lease validation.\n1425|Terminal scrollback and live process memory are not portable state.\n1426|\n1427|Full tmux restore on a Windows computer is a WSL2 feature and uses the Linux\n1428|paths, process model, and provider installation inside that distribution. A\n1429|native Windows provider store and a WSL2 provider store are distinct\n1430|materialization targets.\n1431|\n1432|### 4.4 User services\n1433|\n1434|The background service integration is:\n1435|\n1436|- a launchd agent on macOS;\n1437|- a systemd user unit on Linux and WSL2 where systemd is enabled;\n1438|- otherwise an explicitly installed per-user periodic launcher on WSL2; and\n1439|- a Scheduled Task or per-user service on native Windows.\n1440|\n1441|The service MAY run periodic sync, peer health checks, tombstone\n1442|acknowledgement, stale-process detection, and wrapper restoration. Core commands\n1443|MUST work without it. Service absence MUST degrade freshness, not corrupt\n1444|ownership.\n1445|\n1446|The macOS launchd background control plane and Aqua terminal broker are separate\n1447|roles. The control plane MUST NOT acquire GUI/Keychain authority by proxy and\n1448|MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server. The Aqua broker exposes\n1449|only authenticated, same-user, generation-bound terminal readiness and server\n1450|operations; it does not gain lease, workspace, provider, or replication\n1451|authority.\n1452|\n1453|## 5. Domain records and state machine\n1454|\n1455|### 5.1 Session Record\n1456|\n1457|This subsection defines the immutable Session Record <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1458|variant. It is created exactly once and uses schema\n1459|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-record</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1460|5.1.1 and 5.1.2 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1461|<code>3.0.0</code> variants used by clone and unified-derivation writers; they do\n1462|not mutate or widen the base variant.\n1463|\n1464|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1465|| --- | --- | --- |\n1466|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact schema identifier |\n1467|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | <code>1.0.0</code> |\n(more lines below)"}}}
