{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c559","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e5a-32bc-7443-a1f1-5c57fcb17017"},"sequence":263,"recorded_at":1780531400000521,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"da800a73-e945-4f53-bd35-5e7a4ac47d53"},"task_id":"da800a73-e945-4f53-bd35-5e7a4ac47d53","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"da800a73-e945-4f53-bd35-5e7a4ac47d53","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(2574 line(s) above)\n2575|### 6.5 Configuration 3.0.0 TerminalBackend extension\n2576|\n2577|Configuration 3.0.0 retains every v2 member and replaces only the closed\n2578|<code>terminal</code> table. Its exact members are:\n2579|\n2580|| Key | Default / constraint |\n2581|| --- | --- |\n2582|| <code>backend_id</code> | Platform default for new activation: <code>ax.tmux</code> on macOS/Linux/WSL2 and <code>ax.conpty</code> on Windows; valid registered ID |\n2583|| <code>safe_boundary_timeout_seconds</code> | v2 semantics, integer 1–3,600 |\n2584|| <code>graceful_stop_timeout_seconds</code> | v2 semantics, integer 1–600 |\n2585|| <code>required_capabilities</code> | Sorted unique closed capability names; default platform lane minimum |\n2586|| <code>multiple_input_policy</code> | <code>deny|explicit_allow</code>; default deny |\n2587|| <code>transport_policy</code> | Sorted unique subset of <code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh</code>; default both; relay is not configurable |\n2588|| <code>external_trust</code> | Array of closed executable trust entries |\n2589|| <code>backend_config</code> | Array of closed backend-specific tagged entries |\n2590|\n2591|Each external-trust entry contains exactly backend ID, absolute executable\n2592|path, executable digest, and <code>enabled</code>. PATH-only discovery and a\n2593|digest mismatch fail before probe. Each backend-config entry contains exactly\n2594|backend ID, <code>config_version:semver</code>, and a backend-defined closed\n2595|<code>settings</code> object registered by that exact implementation version.\n2596|An arbitrary blob, raw command/argv, secret, token, endpoint credential,\n2597|unrestricted environment, or environment passthrough is forbidden.\n2598|\n2599|Duplicate IDs or config entries, unknown IDs/settings, ambiguous discovery,\n2600|manifest/probe/config mismatch, unsupported platform, unavailable required\n2601|capability, or untrusted executable fails configuration/activation. Platform\n2602|defaults select only a new Terminal Instance. Restore/resume uses the exact\n2603|prior binding and fails with restore mismatch rather than using the current\n2604|default. Policy may further restrict capabilities/transports but cannot enable\n2605|an unsupported claim.\n2606|\n2607|<code>ax terminal backends list|show|probe|doctor</code> and <code>ax doctor</code>\n2608|MUST safely show sanitized identity, versions, platform, availability,\n2609|capability/evidence status, generation freshness, selection source, and\n2610|remediation. They MUST NOT show native references, sockets/pipes, tokens,\n2611|credentials, auth databases, raw evidence secrets, environment values, or live\n2612|process handles. Inspection is read-only and never activates a backend.\n2613|\n2614|Configuration 1.0.0 and 2.0.0 retain their exact\n2615|<code>terminal.backend=tmux|conpty</code> behavior. Migration to v3 maps only\n2616|those two values as Section 4.E specifies, writes an owner-only backup and\n2617|atomic replacement, and does not alter old bytes. A v1/v2 binary opening v3 is\n2618|read-only diagnostic and MUST NOT discard tables or write a downgraded file.\n2619|\n2620|## 7. Provider plugin protocol\n2621|\n2622|### 7.1 Discovery and trust\n2623|\n2624|Built-in support covers <code>codex</code>, <code>claude</code>,\n2625|<code>gemini</code>, <code>muse</code>, <code>antigravity</code>, and\n2626|<code>pi</code>. External provider executables are named\n2627|<code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code>, where <code>id</code> matches\n2628|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>.\n2629|\n2630|Candidate discovery order is:\n2631|\n2632|1. configured <code>providers.plugin_dirs</code> in listed order;\n2633|2. built-in adapters; then\n2634|3. <code>PATH</code>, only when <code>allow_path_plugins</code> is true.\n2635|\n2636|M0 establishes the versioned plugin wire contracts, internal implementation\n2637|interfaces, and a conformance harness. M0 MUST NOT advertise a public stable\n2638|plugin SDK. A stable public SDK remains deferred until both Codex and Claude\n2639|implementations validate that the boundary is sufficient without provider-\n2640|specific authority leakage or compatibility shims.\n2641|\n2642|The order does not establish precedence. If two candidates—including a built-in\n2643|and an executable—declare the same provider ID, discovery MUST fail with\n2644|<code>invalid_config</code> before either candidate is probed or executed.\n2645|Configuration schema 1.0.0 has no duplicate-selection override; the operator\n2646|must remove or rename one candidate. For each accepted external candidate, the\n2647|canonical absolute executable path and SHA-256 digest MUST be recorded at trust\n2648|time. Symlinks MUST be resolved before comparison, the target MUST be a regular\n2649|file owned by the operator or an administrator-approved identity, and a changed\n2650|path target or digest MUST require renewed trust. Plugins execute with the\n2651|operator's privileges and are inside the trusted-host boundary, but they MUST\n2652|receive only the minimum operation-specific inputs.\n2653|\n2654|### 7.2 Framing and lifecycle\n2655|\n2656|The provider protocol is line-delimited JSON over stdin/stdout with\n2657|<code>protocol = \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\"</code> and\n2658|<code>protocol_version = \"2.0.0\"</code>. Each line MUST be one complete UTF-8\n2659|JSON object no larger than 8 MiB. Stdout MUST contain protocol frames only;\n2660|human diagnostics go to stderr.\n2661|\n2662|<code>ax</code> starts one plugin process per operation. Requests are\n2663|single-flight in v2. After one response, <code>ax</code> closes stdin and the\n2664|plugin MUST exit. Exit 0 requires a successful response. A structured error\n2665|response SHOULD exit 0 because the protocol succeeded; a crash, invalid frame,\n2666|or missing response is a provider-host failure.\n2667|\n2668|Request envelope:\n2669|\n2670|~~~json\n2671|{\n2672|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n2673|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n2674|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ab\",\n2675|  \"operation\": \"doctor\",\n2676|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:05:00.000Z\",\n2677|  \"body\": {\n2678|    \"platform\": \"macos\",\n2679|    \"architecture\": \"arm64\",\n2680|    \"provider_executable\": \"/opt/local/bin/pi\",\n2681|    \"identity\": null\n2682|  }\n2683|}\n2684|~~~\n2685|\n2686|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n2687|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code> UUIDv7,\n2688|<code>operation</code> from the Section 7.5 operation registry,\n2689|<code>deadline</code> timestamp, and the operation-specific <code>body</code>.\n2690|The deadline MUST be in the future when the host writes the frame.\n2691|\n2692|Success envelope:\n2693|\n2694|~~~json\n(more lines below)"}}}
