{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e5a-32bc-7443-a1f1-5c57fcb17017"},"sequence":265,"recorded_at":1780531400000525,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"45bc578a-557d-4117-b36a-1b3b692daf30"},"task_id":"45bc578a-557d-4117-b36a-1b3b692daf30","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"45bc578a-557d-4117-b36a-1b3b692daf30","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(3451 line(s) above)\n3452|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3453|\n3454|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3455|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3456|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3457|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3458|\n3459|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3460|| --- | --- |\n3461|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3462|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3463|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3464|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3465|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3466|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3467|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3468|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3469|\n3470|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3471|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3472|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3473|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3474|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3475|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3476|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3477|\n3478|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3479|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3480|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3481|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3482|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3483|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3484|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3485|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3486|\n3487|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3488|\n3489|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3490|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3491|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3492|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3493|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3494|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3495|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3496|\n3497|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3498|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3499|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3500|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3501|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3502|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3503|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3504|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3505|\n3506|The closed operation registry is:\n3507|\n3508|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3509|| --- | --- |\n3510|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3511|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3512|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3513|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3514|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3515|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3516|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3517|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3518|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3519|\n3520|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3521|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n(more lines below)"}}}
