{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c561","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e5a-32bc-7443-a1f1-5c57fcb17017"},"sequence":267,"recorded_at":1780531400000529,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc"},"call_id":"call_01a06e5ac61a76f19f8814aab46cd5a3","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(1337 line(s) above)\n1338|### 4.1 Terminal backend interface\n1339|\n1340|Every terminal backend MUST implement these semantic operations:\n1341|\n1342|| Operation | Required result |\n1343|| --- | --- |\n1344|| <code>create</code> | With <code>session_id</code> and caller-stable <code>bootstrap_operation_id</code>, create a durable pane/process whose only stable entry point is <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>. |\n1345|| <code>attach</code> | Connect an operator to the local terminal without changing ownership. |\n1346|| <code>status</code> | Report process presence, wrapper state, provider child state, and attachability. |\n1347|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | Stop new operator/provider input while retaining observation. |\n1348|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | Prove the adapter-specific safe boundary or time out. |\n1349|| <code>request-stop</code> | Ask the provider to exit through a version-tested graceful path. |\n1350|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | Terminate a process only for explicit force recovery after preserving diagnostics. |\n1351|| <code>restore</code> | Recreate the wrapper after reboot and consult current ownership before any provider resume. |\n1352|\n1353|The wrapper MUST validate configuration, load the logical session, synchronize\n1354|known lease records when possible, and compare the local fencing token before\n1355|launching a provider. It MUST park safely when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n1356|or unverified.\n1357|\n1358|Terminal creation and the wrapper's first child start are idempotent on\n1359|<code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code>. The backend MUST durably bind\n1360|that pair before child creation. An identical retry returns or reattaches to\n1361|the one recorded wrapper/child; changing the operation for a session still in\n1362|the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. After a lost result,\n1363|<code>status</code> plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one\n1364|child before any start retry. This contract never persists or replicates a PID\n1365|as identity.\n1366|\n1367|### 4.2 tmux backend\n1368|\n1369|On macOS, Linux, and WSL2, the supported durable terminal backend is tmux. Every\n1370|managed pane MUST run:\n1371|\n1372|~~~shell\n1373|ax pane <logical-session-id>\n1374|~~~\n1375|\n1376|It MUST NOT run the raw provider command as the pane's stable command.\n1377|<code>tmux-resurrect</code> plus <code>tmux-continuum</code> MAY recreate local\n1378|tmux layout and invoke the wrapper after reboot. They MUST NOT be described or\n1379|used as cross-host migration.\n1380|\n1381|AX MUST use its dedicated <code>-S</code> server and MUST NOT discover or reuse\n1382|the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name. On macOS, server\n1383|creation is credential-sensitive. A Background caller MUST NOT create a\n1384|credential-dependent tmux server. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon,\n1385|or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and\n1386|its attested AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return\n1387|<code>capability_unavailable</code> with typed realm/readiness details and MUST\n1388|NOT fall back to direct server creation.\n1389|\n1390|<code>launchctl managername</code> is a diagnostic hint only. Conformance\n1391|requires a functional AX sentinel inside the exact tmux server plus a separate\n1392|provider-auth smoke using the selected provider. Evidence MUST bind the exact\n1393|tmux server generation, provider build, and macOS version. Aqua alone and\n1394|sentinel-only evidence are insufficient. Any provider flow requiring GUI\n1395|interaction, Keychain UI, a permission prompt, or other human action fails\n1396|closed until that interaction succeeds in the verified GUI realm.\n1397|\n1398|After restore, the wrapper MUST:\n1399|\n1400|1. read the latest locally known lease;\n1401|2. attempt a mesh lease refresh without blocking forever;\n1402|3. resume locally only if the local host has the winning lease and the required\n1403|   materialization is valid;\n1404|4. offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session in an\n1405|   interactive terminal; or\n1406|5. enter <code>parked</code> without launching the provider in all other cases.\n1407|\n1408|Logout or reboot invalidates unrenewed realm evidence. Without a verified GUI\n1409|realm, recovery MUST remain parked until GUI login re-establishes the broker,\n1410|functional sentinel, provider-auth smoke, and their generation/build/version\n1411|binding. A cached sentinel or prior <code>managername</code> observation MUST\n1412|NOT authorize resume.\n1413|\n1414|### 4.3 Native Windows backend\n1415|\n1416|Native Windows PowerShell MUST use a Windows terminal backend implemented with\n1417|Go process supervision and ConPTY. It MUST support mesh sync, workspace and\n1418|provider materialization, direct/provider resume, task-board open/adopt, remote\n1419|attach, graceful takeover when the provider row passes ConPTY gates, force\n1420|takeover, stop, and continuation.\n1421|\n1422|Native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux or tmux resurrection. A reboot destroys the\n1423|live ConPTY. The user service MUST recreate <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>,\n1424|which resumes from the latest valid checkpoint only after lease validation.\n1425|Terminal scrollback and live process memory are not portable state.\n1426|\n1427|Full tmux restore on a Windows computer is a WSL2 feature and uses the Linux\n1428|paths, process model, and provider installation inside that distribution. A\n1429|native Windows provider store and a WSL2 provider store are distinct\n1430|materialization targets.\n1431|\n1432|### 4.4 User services\n1433|\n1434|The background service integration is:\n1435|\n1436|- a launchd agent on macOS;\n1437|- a systemd user unit on Linux and WSL2 where systemd is enabled;\n1438|- otherwise an explicitly installed per-user periodic launcher on WSL2; and\n1439|- a Scheduled Task or per-user service on native Windows.\n1440|\n1441|The service MAY run periodic sync, peer health checks, tombstone\n1442|acknowledgement, stale-process detection, and wrapper restoration. Core commands\n1443|MUST work without it. Service absence MUST degrade freshness, not corrupt\n1444|ownership.\n1445|\n1446|The macOS launchd background control plane and Aqua terminal broker are separate\n1447|roles. The control plane MUST NOT acquire GUI/Keychain authority by proxy and\n1448|MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server. The Aqua broker exposes\n1449|only authenticated, same-user, generation-bound terminal readiness and server\n1450|operations; it does not gain lease, workspace, provider, or replication\n1451|authority.\n1452|\n1453|## 5. Domain records and state machine\n1454|\n1455|### 5.1 Session Record\n1456|\n1457|This subsection defines the immutable Session Record <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1458|variant. It is created exactly once and uses schema\n1459|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-record</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1460|5.1.1 and 5.1.2 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1461|<code>3.0.0</code> variants used by clone and unified-derivation writers; they do\n1462|not mutate or widen the base variant.\n1463|\n1464|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1465|| --- | --- | --- |\n1466|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact schema identifier |\n1467|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | <code>1.0.0</code> |\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c563","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e5a-32bc-7443-a1f1-5c57fcb17017"},"sequence":268,"recorded_at":1780531400000531,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc"},"call_id":"call_01a06e5ac76371b1818b900470983b40","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(2574 line(s) above)\n2575|### 6.5 Configuration 3.0.0 TerminalBackend extension\n2576|\n2577|Configuration 3.0.0 retains every v2 member and replaces only the closed\n2578|<code>terminal</code> table. Its exact members are:\n2579|\n2580|| Key | Default / constraint |\n2581|| --- | --- |\n2582|| <code>backend_id</code> | Platform default for new activation: <code>ax.tmux</code> on macOS/Linux/WSL2 and <code>ax.conpty</code> on Windows; valid registered ID |\n2583|| <code>safe_boundary_timeout_seconds</code> | v2 semantics, integer 1–3,600 |\n2584|| <code>graceful_stop_timeout_seconds</code> | v2 semantics, integer 1–600 |\n2585|| <code>required_capabilities</code> | Sorted unique closed capability names; default platform lane minimum |\n2586|| <code>multiple_input_policy</code> | <code>deny|explicit_allow</code>; default deny |\n2587|| <code>transport_policy</code> | Sorted unique subset of <code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh</code>; default both; relay is not configurable |\n2588|| <code>external_trust</code> | Array of closed executable trust entries |\n2589|| <code>backend_config</code> | Array of closed backend-specific tagged entries |\n2590|\n2591|Each external-trust entry contains exactly backend ID, absolute executable\n2592|path, executable digest, and <code>enabled</code>. PATH-only discovery and a\n2593|digest mismatch fail before probe. Each backend-config entry contains exactly\n2594|backend ID, <code>config_version:semver</code>, and a backend-defined closed\n2595|<code>settings</code> object registered by that exact implementation version.\n2596|An arbitrary blob, raw command/argv, secret, token, endpoint credential,\n2597|unrestricted environment, or environment passthrough is forbidden.\n2598|\n2599|Duplicate IDs or config entries, unknown IDs/settings, ambiguous discovery,\n2600|manifest/probe/config mismatch, unsupported platform, unavailable required\n2601|capability, or untrusted executable fails configuration/activation. Platform\n2602|defaults select only a new Terminal Instance. Restore/resume uses the exact\n2603|prior binding and fails with restore mismatch rather than using the current\n2604|default. Policy may further restrict capabilities/transports but cannot enable\n2605|an unsupported claim.\n2606|\n2607|<code>ax terminal backends list|show|probe|doctor</code> and <code>ax doctor</code>\n2608|MUST safely show sanitized identity, versions, platform, availability,\n2609|capability/evidence status, generation freshness, selection source, and\n2610|remediation. They MUST NOT show native references, sockets/pipes, tokens,\n2611|credentials, auth databases, raw evidence secrets, environment values, or live\n2612|process handles. Inspection is read-only and never activates a backend.\n2613|\n2614|Configuration 1.0.0 and 2.0.0 retain their exact\n2615|<code>terminal.backend=tmux|conpty</code> behavior. Migration to v3 maps only\n2616|those two values as Section 4.E specifies, writes an owner-only backup and\n2617|atomic replacement, and does not alter old bytes. A v1/v2 binary opening v3 is\n2618|read-only diagnostic and MUST NOT discard tables or write a downgraded file.\n2619|\n2620|## 7. Provider plugin protocol\n2621|\n2622|### 7.1 Discovery and trust\n2623|\n2624|Built-in support covers <code>codex</code>, <code>claude</code>,\n2625|<code>gemini</code>, <code>muse</code>, <code>antigravity</code>, and\n2626|<code>pi</code>. External provider executables are named\n2627|<code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code>, where <code>id</code> matches\n2628|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>.\n2629|\n2630|Candidate discovery order is:\n2631|\n2632|1. configured <code>providers.plugin_dirs</code> in listed order;\n2633|2. built-in adapters; then\n2634|3. <code>PATH</code>, only when <code>allow_path_plugins</code> is true.\n2635|\n2636|M0 establishes the versioned plugin wire contracts, internal implementation\n2637|interfaces, and a conformance harness. M0 MUST NOT advertise a public stable\n2638|plugin SDK. A stable public SDK remains deferred until both Codex and Claude\n2639|implementations validate that the boundary is sufficient without provider-\n2640|specific authority leakage or compatibility shims.\n2641|\n2642|The order does not establish precedence. If two candidates—including a built-in\n2643|and an executable—declare the same provider ID, discovery MUST fail with\n2644|<code>invalid_config</code> before either candidate is probed or executed.\n2645|Configuration schema 1.0.0 has no duplicate-selection override; the operator\n2646|must remove or rename one candidate. For each accepted external candidate, the\n2647|canonical absolute executable path and SHA-256 digest MUST be recorded at trust\n2648|time. Symlinks MUST be resolved before comparison, the target MUST be a regular\n2649|file owned by the operator or an administrator-approved identity, and a changed\n2650|path target or digest MUST require renewed trust. Plugins execute with the\n2651|operator's privileges and are inside the trusted-host boundary, but they MUST\n2652|receive only the minimum operation-specific inputs.\n2653|\n2654|### 7.2 Framing and lifecycle\n2655|\n2656|The provider protocol is line-delimited JSON over stdin/stdout with\n2657|<code>protocol = \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\"</code> and\n2658|<code>protocol_version = \"2.0.0\"</code>. Each line MUST be one complete UTF-8\n2659|JSON object no larger than 8 MiB. Stdout MUST contain protocol frames only;\n2660|human diagnostics go to stderr.\n2661|\n2662|<code>ax</code> starts one plugin process per operation. Requests are\n2663|single-flight in v2. After one response, <code>ax</code> closes stdin and the\n2664|plugin MUST exit. Exit 0 requires a successful response. A structured error\n2665|response SHOULD exit 0 because the protocol succeeded; a crash, invalid frame,\n2666|or missing response is a provider-host failure.\n2667|\n2668|Request envelope:\n2669|\n2670|~~~json\n2671|{\n2672|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n2673|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n2674|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ab\",\n2675|  \"operation\": \"doctor\",\n2676|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:05:00.000Z\",\n2677|  \"body\": {\n2678|    \"platform\": \"macos\",\n2679|    \"architecture\": \"arm64\",\n2680|    \"provider_executable\": \"/opt/local/bin/pi\",\n2681|    \"identity\": null\n2682|  }\n2683|}\n2684|~~~\n2685|\n2686|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n2687|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code> UUIDv7,\n2688|<code>operation</code> from the Section 7.5 operation registry,\n2689|<code>deadline</code> timestamp, and the operation-specific <code>body</code>.\n2690|The deadline MUST be in the future when the host writes the frame.\n2691|\n2692|Success envelope:\n2693|\n2694|~~~json\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c565","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e5a-32bc-7443-a1f1-5c57fcb17017"},"sequence":269,"recorded_at":1780531400000533,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc"},"call_id":"call_01a06e5ac8ba77e38758fa179ad556bd","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(3451 line(s) above)\n3452|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3453|\n3454|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3455|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3456|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3457|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3458|\n3459|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3460|| --- | --- |\n3461|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3462|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3463|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3464|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3465|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3466|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3467|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3468|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3469|\n3470|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3471|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3472|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3473|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3474|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3475|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3476|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3477|\n3478|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3479|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3480|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3481|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3482|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3483|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3484|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3485|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3486|\n3487|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3488|\n3489|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3490|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3491|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3492|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3493|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3494|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3495|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3496|\n3497|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3498|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3499|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3500|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3501|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3502|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3503|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3504|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3505|\n3506|The closed operation registry is:\n3507|\n3508|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3509|| --- | --- |\n3510|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3511|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3512|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3513|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3514|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3515|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3516|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3517|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3518|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3519|\n3520|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3521|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
