{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cfe1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e5a-32bc-7443-a1f1-5c57fcb17017"},"sequence":1611,"recorded_at":1780531400003217,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d4680851-7ee4-46f3-b9ae-940cf14558fc"},"call_id":"call_01a06e63aeac7890af707ffe558ddf29","text":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-03\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-04\n+\n+### 2147 — Terminal backend registry: the two board-disclosed findings decided without inventing constraints\n+\n+- SCOPE: new `internal/terminalbackend/` (registry, canonical IDs, version tuples, trust, duplicate/drift refusal, restore binding, §7.A descriptor check), `internal/config/validation.go` wiring, new `internal/config/terminal_registry_wiring_test.go`. TASK-260830-2xdt8t, spec v0.5.0 §4.B, §4.1, §6.5, §7.A. Commit 8cb29ea, signed, story branch, worktree clean, not pushed.\n+- DECISION (finding 1): `required_capabilities` keeps its empty default. SPEC.md:2585 (\"default platform lane minimum\") is the sole occurrence of the phrase in the 12,665-line SPEC; no per-platform minimum set is enumerated anywhere, so implementing one would invent a constraint. Empty enables nothing per SPEC.md:2604-2605 (\"Policy may further restrict capabilities/transports but cannot enable an unsupported claim\"); per-operation capability dependencies (§4.C/§4.D) still gate activation. No code change.\n+- DECISION (finding 2): §6.2 \"terminal backend MUST be conpty\" on native Windows (SPEC.md:2415-2418) governs the v1/v2 `terminal.backend` field and is enforced across versions; added the missing legacy-arm pin `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` (v1 tmux-on-Windows refuses, conpty loads to `ax.conpty`). Deliberately NOT extended to third-party IDs: §6.5 admits them as \"valid registered ID\" with manifest-bound platforms.\n+- EVIDENCE: `go test ./...` exit 0 (14 packages), `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean; terminalbackend 89.3%, config 94.7% statement coverage. Every refusal gate narrowed (grammar widened one rule at a time; drift changes one record member at a time); `TestErrorPredicatesAreExclusive` proves one wire code per refusal; duplicate/drift refusals assert the admitted record is unchanged. Wire codes verified against the pinned catalog vocabulary in-test.\n+- BOUND: registry is process-local memory — no durable-state crash-recovery evidence applies; duplicate/drift non-clobber assertions are the idempotency evidence. Manifest/Probe schemas, capability evidence, lifecycle ops, legacy v0.4.3 translation are sibling tasks, untouched.\n+\n+## 2026-09-03\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/LOGBOOK.md","added":16,"removed":6},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
